<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sephardic Jews</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Sephardim</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sephardic <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jews">Jews</a> are the Jewish communities descended from those of medieval <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> and Portugal, expelled in 1492 and 1497. Many settled in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-africa">North Africa</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Netherlands</a>, and from there in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> and English <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caribbean">Caribbean</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guianas">Guianas</a>. They brought <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sugar-plantation">sugar</a> and trading expertise to colonies such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/suriname">Suriname</a> and Curaçao, where Mikvé Israel-Emanuel is the oldest surviving synagogue in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/americas">Americas</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sephardic-jews.jpg" alt="Sephardic Jews" width="320" height="429" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Alfred Dehodencq · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:F%C3%AAte_juive_%C3%A0_T%C3%A9touan,_Alfred_Dehodencq,_1865.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
